.TH SERVE 1 "October 2026" "SPP Enterprise" "SPP CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
serve \- Start the sovereign SPP HTTP web server interactively
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B php spp.php serve
[\fB\-\-host\fR=\fIip\fR]
[\fB\-\-port\fR=\fIport\fR]
[\fB\-\-app\fR=\fIname\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBserve\fR boots SPP's standalone pure-PHP HTTP server fronted by the sovereign router (\fBspp/router.php\fR). It operates completely independently of Apache, Nginx, or external web servers, handling dynamic MVC routing, static asset delivery, security guards, and the SPPAdmin workbench with real-time terminal output.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-host\fR=\fIip\fR
Network interface IP to bind (default: 0.0.0.0 for LAN and local access).
.TP
\fB\-\-port\fR=\fIport\fR
Listening TCP port (default: 8000; use 80 for standard HTTP).
.TP
\fB\-\-app\fR=\fIname\fR
Application context to boot by default.
.SH UNDER THE HOOD
Spawns PHP built-in web server with sovereign router \fBspp/router.php\fR, serving static files and routing dynamic requests to \fBpublic/index.php\fR.
